  "source": "Dubai Land Department transactions export (Kaggle mirror zainabhejairi/dubai-real-estates-1969-2023, DLD_Transactions.csv)",
  "provenance": "UNOFFICIAL third-party mirror of a DLD export. The file is exactly 1,048,575 rows, which is Excel's 1,048,576-row ceiling, so it is a TRUNCATED copy of the registry. Coverage ends in 2023.",
  "period": "2010–2023",
  "minSalesPerYear": 30,
  "method": "2023 median price per m2 against the mean of that community's annual medians from 2010 to 2022. Positive means the community is trading above its own long-run norm. Requires at least 6 scored years.",
  "limitation": "Measures a community against its OWN history only — it carries no income or rent anchor, so it says nothing about affordability, and a structurally improving area can sit permanently above its own past. Results outside -60%–150% are discarded as unit-mix artefacts.",
